    LLM: "Game: Twist'em. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.",
    Player: "Twist'em (Double-Hand Dominoes) is a casino banking game played with a double-six domino set. Each player and the banker receive three tiles and arrange them into a top hand and a bottom hand (pip totals mod 10, nine high). Players bet against the banker; both hands must outrank the banker's two hands to win. Based on Pai Gow but with Western dominoes.",
    objective: "Form two hands (top and bottom) that respectively outrank the banker's two hands; baccarat-style scoring (pip total mod 10, nine high).",
    gameplay: 'Players bet; each receives three tiles and arranges them in a line to form top and bottom hand (totals mod 10). Tiles placed face-down. Banker exposes three tiles and arranges similarly. Compare: player top vs banker top, player bottom vs banker bottom. Both player hands win or one wins and one ties = player wins even money; one wins one loses = push; otherwise player loses. Banker wins ties.',
